[Music]  i see a striking similarity between  music and code  [Music]  when you're producing music or when  you're making music that product that  you're making is a stream of bits it's  ones and zeros and every single action  you take every stroke of the guitar  every conversation you have in the  studio affects how those bits come out  i'm doing two things that i really love  to do and i think that they fuel each  other  my name is brandon tory i'm a musician  and a senior engineer at google working  on ai  as a teenager i lived in a homeless  shelter i met a lot of kids from that  walk of life  i grew up a couple blocks down from  where there was a lot of drug activity  and things like that and a lot of my  friends went to that so obviously that  was a challenge i was like man i want to  get into music i want to do these other  things  when i was living in this shelter one of  the things i brought with me was this  computer that i had built from parts  that i found around the neighborhood and  i spray painted it black and one of the  things i was doing was coding i started  to live this double life where i was  working as an engineer and then i would  come back put out music and do these  things and trying to balance my life as  an artist and my life as an engineer  separately  once again i want to thank everybody for  coming out tonight i'm gonna play the  records for you guys i'm not expecting  you to stand still you know let's have a  good time i appreciate you guys thank  you  first time i played music it felt like  you get this sense of understanding  [Music]  and so what happens is you start to rap  you get in these freestyle ciphers or  these battles or these music sessions  and everybody's really just exchanging  their story and you start to realize  we're really not that different and  music just made it feel very very  obvious and very very powerful me and  benny got a joke when he showed me  diamond chains she gonna take forever  shipping i'm gonna take forever pain  first six months a minute late a friend  of mine said hey man this is contest  with timberland i think you should enter  it and so i just entered it and then one  day i got a call i picked up my phone in  this timber  timberland is arguably the best producer  of all time right next to dr dre and  some of the other legends and for me  that just felt like such a breakthrough  i think all independent artists could  relate to that because we all take this  risk and this and this jump to say man  we want to be creative we want to create  our art and you go through this grind  period where you just don't know if  you're even making any progress at all  and so to have tim call me and say man i  love what you're doing that gave me this  huge surge of energy to keep fighting  and to keep creating  [Music]  my long-term goal will always be to be a  creator  [Music]  all dreams and all things that you're  trying to accomplish have certain  qualities in common you're trying to  constantly create something from nothing  and whether or not that involves coding  or music or any of the tools at my  disposal i'm willing to use those to  create better experiences  [Music]

